#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/7ff0aef4e202f553ffab02ef0af31aec72593f02  ("gfx/nvn: publish coherent presentation-time and display-link history snapshots (PR #2194)")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-23 02:18 +0800; Co-authored-by: Adam Kratch
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why: the drawable callbacks, the queue-drop paths and the timing readers used g_pres and g_link_ring with no synchronization: a data race, torn reads across ticket / timestamp
#   fields, a wrapped entry overwritten while read (upstream PR #2194).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m, new nvn_present_history.h; new tests t_present_history, present-history-tsan): both rings behind a private leaf mutex, older generations and
#   ticket 0 rejected.
# Adapted: three hunks by hand (this tree drops queued presents inline in two places). The .github workflow hunk not taken. Games: every game. Switches: none.
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_present_history 11 checks + 48,000 concurrent publications (also under TSan, `make present-history-tsan`), t_present_rescue, t_present_keep, t_present_crop; in HOST_TESTS.
# NOT run on a device.
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0530, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

